  (text "NMR TX (section B) — AD9834 DDS + reconstruction filter + OPA564 power stage -> TX" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 14 0) (effects (font (size 3 3) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "cadcc819-ae10-5930-a055-9ba69126ae84"))
  (text "DDS: AD9834BRUZ, MCLK = CLK0_MCLK = 50.000 MHz from the Si5351A on the RX sheet; df = f_MCLK / 2^28 = 0.186 Hz per LSB. R801 6.80 k on FS ADJUST -> I_OUT,FS = 18 x 1.20 V / 6.80 k = 3.18 mA;" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 19 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2e8edb54-625b-51f1-a1db-2e9668424a9b"))
  (text "R802 / R803 200 R loads -> 0.636 V pp at IOUT, inside the 0.8 V output-compliance limit (datasheet pins 19/20). C807 20 pF C0G on IOUT prevents clock feedthrough. FSELECT tied to DGND (frequency selected by the FSEL control bit)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 22.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "18da2b03-4862-5d80-9d18-95b809ba553c"))
  (text "Reconstruction filter: singly-terminated 3rd-order Butterworth, f_c = 3 MHz, source resistance = the 200 R DAC load, prototype g = 1.5 / 1.3333 / 0.5 -> C808 390 pF, L801 15 uH (LQH32DN150K53L, SRF 26 MHz), C809 130 pF." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 25.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c920dedf-4aca-5d94-b634-6cc0518f411c"))
  (text "The nearest image at 48 MHz is down (48/3)^3 = 72 dB; passband -0.05 dB at 2 MHz, flat at 89 kHz. C810 1 uF couples into the power stage (f_HP = 3.2 Hz against the 100 k || 100 k bias divider)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 28.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7f980624-ed13-565c-8465-be9be42bcc53"))
  (text "Power stage: SINGLE supply +VEXT (7-18 V), V- = GND. E/S, VDIG and both flags are referenced to V-, so V- = GND lets 3.3 V logic drive them directly; on +-12 V every one of them would need an optocoupler (SBOS372E Fig. 38)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 31.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "94ebff7b-63da-573b-8ec1-5ac9d574ff77"))
  (text "Gain: non-inverting, R807 6.49 k over R808 270 R -> G = 25.0 (15.9 V pp = +-7.95 V = 5.6 mA into the 1419 R coil = t90 417 us at 89.4 kHz). Alternative R808 stuffings: 1.00 k -> G 7.49 and 3.32 k -> G 2.95 for the >= 1 MHz settings." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 35 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "769c9c2d-7a78-5a90-95a7-0508a7ca9e4b"))
  (text "Protection: R809 11.0 k on ISET -> I_LIM = 1.50 A (NEVER leave ISET open — the datasheet says an open pin damages the device). R810 10 k beats the internal 100 k pull-up on E/S: 3.3 x 10/110 = 0.30 V < 0.8 V = shut down until firmware raises TX_EN." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 38.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ad615f61-8623-56a2-97c8-0fdbb54e0f40"))
  (text "D801 / D802 SS54 clamp the output to +VEXT and to GND; R813 4.7 R 1 W isolates it; R814 / C817 (10 R + 10 nF) is the datasheet snubber; C818 10 uF blocks the 9 V mid-rail out of the coil (Z = 0.18 R at 89 kHz). JP802 + R815/R816 = the -20 dB pad option." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 41.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "32b8a3c6-7a6a-5cd0-9c49-79e414b4e77a"))
  (text "Sequencing (SBOS372E Fig. 36): VDIG (+3V3, from USB) must come up BEFORE V+ (+VEXT, bench supply) — silkscreen note next to the external power input. PowerPAD pin 21 = V- = GND, pad DOWN on the ground pour with a via array (theta_JA 33 C/W)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 44.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "675b69a0-00cb-5810-ab6b-2f1a4a35c0eb"))
  (text "Grounding (re-spec 8.1): the AD9834 AGND and DGND are tied together AT THE DEVICE and belong to the AGND pour; AVDD/DVDD come from +3V3 through FB801 (local rail +3V3D). The OPA564 and the coil return are on GND. C810 is the only signal crossing the two pours." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 47.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "482229be-83fd-5fb6-a922-dd370850a3a4"))
  (text "+3V3 -> FB801 -> +3V3D: AVDD (C801) and DVDD (C802) 100 nF each plus C806 10 uF bulk, all returned to AGND" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 105 77 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4e945bbf-3bc7-5184-b037-1f6dbb3f8f97"))
  (text "R817 / R818: 10 k pull-downs (RESET is active HIGH on the AD9834)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 178 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "56374a92-c8fb-57e2-90a2-2c7a9921dba0"))
  (text "Both lines go to TCA9535 spare pins P1.5 / P1.6 — global labels until" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 181.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e5e4eab5-2294-5d38-aab2-4c4e73e2b470"))
  (text "the expander sheet claims them." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 184.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e9aed6a0-77e1-58d6-860e-f17639160d6f"))
  (text "R801 6.80 k: I_OUT,FS = 18 x V_REFOUT / R_SET = 18 x 1.20 / 6800 = 3.18 mA. C805 decouples COMP to AVDD (datasheet Fig. 1)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 193 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "fe3d8efa-e7de-51a0-b363-fec3ba530c70"))
  (text "AGND (18) and DGND (7) tied at the device; both on the AGND pour (re-spec 8.1)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 138.43 171 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2d879699-6de6-509d-841e-3bbfa97bc6eb"))
  (text "Singly-terminated 3rd-order Butterworth, f_c = 3 MHz, R = 200 R (the DAC load doubles as the filter source):" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 152.4 135 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4437fcbd-18fe-5315-b763-89169f6e875e"))
  (text "C808 = 1.5/(2 pi f_c R) = 398 pF, L801 = 1.3333 R/(2 pi f_c) = 14.1 uH, C809 = 0.5/(2 pi f_c R) = 133 pF." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 152.4 138.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ecd0468d-8469-5fa2-a288-9aa902a134d4"))
  (text "C810 is the ONLY connection between the AGND (DDS) domain and the GND (power-stage) domain." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 152.4 141.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d252eb33-bbb0-5a26-9643-320e95287004"))
  (text "Mid-rail bias: V_mid = VEXT/2 = 9.0 V at 18 V; 100 k || 100 k = 50 k filtered by C811/C812 (f = 0.32 Hz)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 160 182.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "84eba1ce-bc0e-5dd5-8579-56425f8a5b40"))
  (text "FB802 (120 R @ 100 MHz, 3 A) isolates the OPA564 V+ branch from the +VEXT input; C815 47 uF + C816 100 nF sit after it, at the V+ pins (SBOS372E Fig. 35)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 226 85 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e7582e58-6660-55ae-84e9-09c4a251edbc"))
  (text "Single +VEXT 7-18 V; total supply <= 24 V, absolute max 26 V. D801 clamps the output to +VEXT_TX, the same post-bead node." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 226 88.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4293811b-134b-52dd-9d5e-cf6063ee9b32"))
  (text "V- (1/10/11/20), V-PWR (13/14) and the PowerPAD EP (21) are all GND:" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 160 186 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "22c8bac8-75e1-5ae1-a116-523643e656e3"))
  (text "pad DOWN onto the ground pour with a via array, theta_JA 33 C/W." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 160 189.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4ae45f9e-9dc3-5b86-946d-7e8e7d9773e3"))
  (text "I_FLAG / T_FLAG are push-pull CMOS referenced to V- = GND, so R811 / R812 are DNP" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 300 178 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "14a0e16e-d4b2-5830-9c8f-db79a0d47830"))
  (text "footprints only. Both flags go to TCA9535 spare inputs; poll them after every pulse." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 300 181.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "cb90fc48-2fb7-574b-8634-6029a5c67ff4"))
  (text "G = 1 + R807/R808 = 1 + 6490/270 = 25.0. C813 blocks DC in the gain leg, so the DC gain is 1 and the output" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 214 212 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7820d40f-58e9-5ed3-8373-e2dfacce2d18"))
  (text "sits at V_mid (f_HP = 5.9 Hz). JP801 (1-2 bridged) opens the gain leg for a unity-gain bring-up; pad 3 is a" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 214 215.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "79d4897d-ff7e-55f7-9cfc-b50b29970883"))
  (text "spare for an external gain resistor." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 214 218.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "34fff39d-536d-55bb-92c2-e1c558b56a8b"))
  (text "-20 dB pad: 100/(910+100) = 0.099 into a high-Z load." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 303 96 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a58e5622-a41f-5c17-a957-372b0303101a"))
  (text "TX leaves this sheet as a global label -> panel link J6 pins 19 and 21 (AGND on 20 and 22)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 300 195 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "67c8bc82-9577-5c71-8204-a1e02e187337"))
  (text "-> the TX SMA and the 2P screw terminal on the panel. Route TX and its return as a close pair," (exclude_from_sim no) (at 300 198.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "fa29110f-de6f-56a4-b7a1-efb981ed90dc"))
  (text "loop area < 1 cm2; up to 1 A of coil current must never share copper with the receiver pour." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 300 201.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a9a482f2-5322-589d-900b-528c049d0052"))
  (text "Level plan from 0.636 V pp at the DDS output (re-spec 2.3). Top row = the 89.4 kHz NMR setting: +-7.95 V into 1419 R = 5.6 mA = t90 417 us." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 198 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "44c6fdfb-d4e3-5559-9fc9-92520ff1486d"))
  (text "Firmware (re-spec 9.1 / 9.3): hold DDS_RESET high while writing, B28 = 1, PIN/SW set for hardware PSELECT; the carrier free-runs and is gated ONLY by TX_EN." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 222 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "79dee877-9589-5d83-b4c5-1cf7fa642d74"))
  (text "TX_EN must be low except during a pulse — for the thermal budget as much as for receiver blanking (quiescent 39 mA x 18 V = 0.70 W, shutdown 5 mA = 0.09 W)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 225.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0357b5b3-6709-57b1-8a8a-a6c5a0f34416"))
